### 1. Issue or feature description
There's no option to disable gfd from the helm chart and make it apply on the clusterPolicy object that is created.

For example the following command 
```
$ helm install --wait --generate-name  --set nfd.enabled=false --set driver.enabled=false --set toolkit.version=v1.10.0-centos7 --set gfd.enabled=false  nvidia/gpu-operator
```
Does not disable the option for the clusterPolicy object 

```
$ kubectl get clusterpolicy -o yaml | grep -A10 gfd
    gfd:
      env:
      - name: GFD_SLEEP_INTERVAL
        value: 60s
      - name: GFD_FAIL_ON_INIT_ERROR
        value: "true"
      image: gpu-feature-discovery
      imagePullPolicy: IfNotPresent
      repository: nvcr.io/nvidia
      version: v0.6.1-ubi8
 ``` 
 
 and the pods are unnecessarily created
 
 ```
 $ kubectl get po
NAME                                       READY   STATUS                  RESTARTS      AGE
gpu-feature-discovery-54vbc                1/1     Running                 0             2m3s
gpu-operator-7c4f4f7b54-z7xlr              1/1     Running                 0             22m
``` 
 
