> The default rootDir of kubelet is `var/lib/kubelet/pod-resources`. But usually we will specify a custom path for rootDir of kubelet likely `/home/kubelet` which is on data disk.

Now  DCGM uses the fixed path `var/lib/kubelet/pod-resources`  as value of [volMountSockPath](https://github.com/NVIDIA/gpu-operator/blob/adceb5ac46c8125ccde13570541db5f1c9c8a302/controllers/object_controls.go#L1536). In this case, the metrics collected by dcgm-exporter would not contain the name of pod.
```go
// controllers/object_controls.go
volMountSockName, volMountSockPath := "pod-gpu-resources", "/var/lib/kubelet/pod-resources"
```


So could DCGM spec add a field named `kubeletRootDir` in [DCGMExporterSpec](https://github.com/NVIDIA/gpu-operator/blob/e9b7ec16203987508eddc048fe82a4c44d3b392a/api/nvidia/v1/clusterpolicy_types.go#L853) to support to specify the custom rootDir of kubelet?
```go
// /api/nvidia/v1/clusterpolicy_types.go
type DCGMExporterSpec struct {
        KubeletRootDir string `json:"kubeletRootDir,omitempty"`
}

// controllers/object_controls.go
volMountSockName, volMountSockPath := "pod-gpu-resources", "/var/lib/kubelet/pod-resources"
if config.DCGM.KubeletRootDir != "" {
      volMountSockPath = config.DCGM.KubeletRootDir + "/pod-resources"
}
```

Waiting for your response.

