In kubevirt-gpu-device-plugin, the discovery code groups VFIO-bound GPUs by IOMMU group and registers them without any topology metadata, each `pluginapi.Device` is created with only ID and Health.

The device ID seen in pod-resource API is IOMMU group ID, and numa group is omitted. so kubelet has nothing to expose for NUMA and uses the opaque IOMMU IDs 

In the following example which is read from pod-resouce API, the nvidia-sandbox-device-plugin, installed by the GPU Operator for KubeVirt physical GPU passthrough, reports the device ID using the IOMMU group instead of the PCI BDF. Neither it reports NUMA node info for this device. This behavior differs from the legacy device plugin — for instance, the sriov-network-device-plugin for nvidia.com/ib_pf , which reports device IDs as PCI BDFs.

```json
  "pod": {
    "namespace": "tenant-d",
    "name": "virt-launcher-testvm-21300-hlflt",
    "containers": [
      {
        "name": "compute",
        "devices": [
          {
            "resourceName": "nvidia.com/PGPU",
            "deviceIds": [
              "94"
            ]
          },
          {
            "resourceName": "nvidia.com/ib_pf",
            "deviceIds": [
              "0000:08:00.0"
            ],
            "numaNodes": [
              0
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "name": "hook-sidecar-0",
        "devices": null
      }
    ]
  } 
```
To better support topology awareness and readiness from pod resource API, there need to expose allocated GPU BDF and NUMA info.

